hw/sh4: ze0 serial receive timeout, SCIF interrupts, DMA receive ring (M8.H39)

Makes a host peer on a SCIF chardev reach the NK1 serial driver:
sh_serial SCIF accepts input up to the free FIFO slots and sets SCLSR.TO
after an idle line (ERI); ERI, TXI and TEI of a channel with a chardev go
to the channel's INTEVT; the HPB-DMAC receive ring keeps running across
pages, with DDASR/DTCSR live and DSTSR bit 5 naming the current page, as
serial_scif.dll's receive handler expects.  ZE0_SCIF_TRACE=scifN prints
SCR/LSR/timeout events of that channel to stderr.

Applies after ze0-h01-serial-chardevs.patch.  Record:
docs/experiments/EXP-2026-11-22-M8.H35-sci3-display-link.md

